---
description: Preserve Chrome layout architecture and state ownership
alwaysApply: true
---

# Chrome Layout Architecture

- Keep `ChromeLayout` thin: composition shell + panel slots, no heavy panel prop forwarding.
- Child layout pieces (for example `ChromeEdgePanel`) should read app state via `useAppStore` and shared controller context.
- Prefer geometry-derived panel config from one source of truth (`position`/edge mapping) over duplicated per-panel props.
- Keep resize/drag orchestration in dedicated controller/hook modules, not inline in layout render components.
- Use global layout patch actions for chrome dimensions/collapse state; avoid local duplicated state for these values.

# Implementation Guardrails

- When adding new chrome sections, derive border/collapse/resize behavior from edge position mappings.
- Avoid reintroducing broad prop drilling (`onResize*`, collapse booleans, border classes) through multiple component levels.
